WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:04.130
[Helicopter rotor sound]

00:29.113 --> 00:32.408
What's that?
— cheat sheet Faraday drew for me.

00:32.492 --> 00:35.286
You don't know where your boat is?

00:35.370 --> 00:36.829
I know where it is.

00:49.634 --> 00:52.512
Why are you flying directly
into the thunderhead?

00:52.595 --> 00:54.889
Why don't you just sit back
and let me do my job?

00:54.973 --> 00:57.058
[Wind howling]

01:02.522 --> 01:03.773
[Thunderclap]

01:03.856 --> 01:04.899
Is that Penelope?

01:07.026 --> 01:10.446
She told Charlie she didn't know
about this boat, correct?

01:11.656 --> 01:14.033
What do you expect to find
when you get there?

01:14.117 --> 01:15.576
Answers.

01:15.660 --> 01:17.120
[Wind howling]

01:32.385 --> 01:33.386
Damn it!

01:37.056 --> 01:40.101
[Beeping]

01:46.149 --> 01:48.651
[Man] On your sodding feet!

01:48.735 --> 01:50.695
Move, move, move!

01:52.905 --> 01:55.325
What are you waiting for, hume?

02:00.788 --> 02:02.665
What's the matter, hume?

02:02.749 --> 02:05.001
Did you not hear me?

02:05.084 --> 02:08.004
I'm sorry, sir.
I was having a dream, sir.

02:08.087 --> 02:09.839
You were having a dream, were you?

02:09.922 --> 02:13.593
What were you dreaming about?
That it took you so sodding long

02:13.676 --> 02:15.636
to get to your Mark?!

02:18.514 --> 02:19.932
I was in a helicopter, sir.

02:21.059 --> 02:23.478
And there was a storm, sir, and...

02:23.603 --> 02:27.607
And... I don't remember the rest, sir.

02:28.733 --> 02:32.028
Well, at least it was
a bloody military dream.

02:34.030 --> 02:36.657
Right! All of you!

02:36.741 --> 02:39.452
In the yard, four minutes!

02:39.535 --> 02:43.873
And you can thank private hume
for having to do it in double time.

02:43.956 --> 02:45.792
Move!

02:45.875 --> 02:47.502
[Man] One, two... — [men] Three!

02:47.585 --> 02:48.878
One, two, three... — four!

02:48.961 --> 02:50.963
One, two, three... — five!

02:51.089 --> 02:53.341
One hundred crunches.

02:53.424 --> 02:55.176
Go, go, go, go, go!

02:56.094 --> 02:58.179
One, two, three...

02:58.262 --> 03:00.556
I hope your dream
was worth this, mate.

03:00.640 --> 03:02.892
Sorry, pal. Just...

03:02.975 --> 03:06.729
I've never had a dream so vivid.
It was like I was actually there.

03:06.813 --> 03:09.232
You got something to say, hume?

03:09.315 --> 03:10.650
I asked you a question!

03:15.405 --> 03:16.906
We're almost through it.

03:16.989 --> 03:18.491
I see daylight.

03:23.996 --> 03:26.249
What do you think you're doing?
Desmond.

03:26.332 --> 03:27.792
Hey, you all right?

03:29.001 --> 03:30.002
Who are you?

03:31.629 --> 03:33.673
[Shouting] How do you know my name?

03:54.277 --> 03:55.528
Here you go.

04:01.492 --> 04:04.287
All right, they took off a day ago.

04:04.370 --> 04:07.540
Why haven't we heard from them?
— I'm gonna tell you again,

04:07.623 --> 04:09.792
as I've been telling you, I don't know!

04:09.876 --> 04:12.962
You heard the same thing as I did
when we called the boat.

04:13.045 --> 04:16.799
What makes you think I know anything?
— because you're not worried.

04:16.883 --> 04:19.385
Excuse me?
— your boat's 40 miles off the coast.

04:19.510 --> 04:22.388
It should've taken them, what,
20 minutes to get there?

04:22.472 --> 04:23.806
Why aren't you worried?

04:23.890 --> 04:26.434
Should I wring my hands together

04:26.517 --> 04:30.104
and whisper a prayer on their behalf?
— hey, hey, hey. Come on.

04:30.188 --> 04:32.648
Maybe we should just tell them.

04:34.650 --> 04:35.985
Tell us what?

04:36.068 --> 04:39.906
Dan, let's not confuse anyone.

04:39.989 --> 04:44.160
Well, Daniel,
maybe if you talk real slow,

04:44.243 --> 04:45.912
we'll be able to follow.

04:49.665 --> 04:53.336
Your perception of how long
your friends have been gone...

04:54.420 --> 04:58.633
It's not necessarily how long
they've actually been gone.

05:00.593 --> 05:03.054
What does that mean?
— this is a mistake.

05:04.180 --> 05:06.182
It'll be fine, it'll be fine.

05:06.265 --> 05:08.768
As long as frank flew
on the bearings I gave him.

05:08.893 --> 05:11.771
If he stayed on it, it'll be fine.

05:11.854 --> 05:13.523
And what if he didn't?

05:14.774 --> 05:17.527
Then there might be side effects.

05:20.905 --> 05:22.114
We're at 2,000 feet. Sit!

05:22.198 --> 05:24.033
What am I doing here?
— what's going on?

05:24.116 --> 05:26.869
Something's wrong with Desmond.
— hold him in his seat!

05:26.953 --> 05:28.829
I'm trying! — let go of me!

05:28.955 --> 05:31.749
Keep him away from the stick!
We'll be there in two minutes!

06:11.247 --> 06:13.374
[Thud]

06:22.174 --> 06:24.093
What are you doing back?
Who are they?

06:24.176 --> 06:25.678
Survivors of 815.

06:27.096 --> 06:30.224
You dropped them here.
What the hell were you thinking?

06:31.017 --> 06:32.810
Where am I? — just take it easy.

06:32.893 --> 06:35.104
Who are you people?
What am I doing here?

06:35.187 --> 06:36.939
Who are you? — my friend has...

06:37.023 --> 06:39.108
I'm not your friend! I don't know you!

06:39.191 --> 06:41.360
I don't know you!

06:42.570 --> 06:45.698
When did he start doing this?
— he was fine when we took off.

06:45.781 --> 06:49.452
We hit some weather... Faraday said
as long as I stayed on the vector...

06:51.704 --> 06:54.749
Wait, wait, wait.
What's your name, my friend?

06:56.208 --> 06:58.377
Sayid. — ok, Sayid.

06:58.461 --> 07:00.921
We're gonna take your buddy
down to the sick bay.

07:01.005 --> 07:03.716
I'm going with him.
— let a doctor look at him first

07:03.841 --> 07:05.509
then you can come down.

07:05.593 --> 07:07.219
You got my word on that, ok?

07:15.311 --> 07:17.313
All right. — listen to me.

07:17.396 --> 07:20.650
This is a mistake, right?
I don't know these people.

07:20.733 --> 07:23.235
I understand.
— no, this is wrong!

07:23.319 --> 07:26.322
I'm not supposed to be here!

07:26.405 --> 07:29.075
[Man] Twenty, 21, 22...

07:29.158 --> 07:31.661
“Here?" here what?

07:31.744 --> 07:34.455
What the hell are you doing
on your feet?

07:34.538 --> 07:36.999
Are you finished with your crunches

07:37.083 --> 07:38.584
because you want to run?!

07:38.668 --> 07:42.588
Right! Squad, on yourfeet!

07:44.674 --> 07:46.342
Right face!

07:46.425 --> 07:49.845
Ten kilometers! Go, go, go, go, go!

07:49.929 --> 07:52.973
Get moving, or so help me
I'll kill you myself!

07:55.434 --> 07:57.895
[Thunderclap]

07:59.980 --> 08:02.233
What the hell's the matter
with you, des?

08:02.316 --> 08:04.360
If I told you, you'd think I was crazy.

08:04.443 --> 08:06.904
I already know you're crazy.

08:08.072 --> 08:12.201
This morning, when I was
in the yard doing crunches...

08:16.455 --> 08:18.249
What do you mean you "left?"

08:20.126 --> 08:23.003
I was on a boat.

08:23.087 --> 08:26.298
And then I was back here,
right where I started.

08:26.382 --> 08:28.551
Des, if you're trying to get tossed...

08:28.634 --> 08:30.678
Billy, I'm telling you the truth, man.

08:33.139 --> 08:36.058
Who else was on this... boat?

08:36.142 --> 08:38.102
Anyone you recognize?

08:40.187 --> 08:41.480
Penny.

08:44.859 --> 08:47.361
There was a photo.
Penny was in the photo.

08:47.445 --> 08:51.157
Wha...?! Oi, des! Where are you going?

08:51.240 --> 08:54.326
[Men shouting marches]

09:00.916 --> 09:02.626
Thanks for this morning, hume.

09:08.632 --> 09:11.302
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Watch your step.

09:12.178 --> 09:14.764
Watch it. Watch your step. Take it easy.

09:16.432 --> 09:17.475
I'm not here.

09:17.558 --> 09:20.019
This... this isn't happening.

09:20.102 --> 09:23.898
You are here, and this is happening.

09:24.023 --> 09:27.777
Look, we're gonna take care of you.
— what am I doing here?

09:27.860 --> 09:31.113
It's all right. You're gonna be ok.
— who are you people?

09:31.197 --> 09:34.867
Well, my name is keamy,
and this is Omar.

09:34.950 --> 09:38.370
I'm from Vegas, he's from Florida.
But as for where we are...

09:38.496 --> 09:40.289
We last ported in Fiji.

09:41.499 --> 09:44.210
So at least we know
we're still in the pacific.

09:50.549 --> 09:53.469
All right, my friend.
You just relax, ok?

09:53.552 --> 09:54.970
We're gonna go get the doc,

09:55.054 --> 09:57.640
and he's gonna want to ask you
some questions

09:57.723 --> 10:00.601
to help us sort all this out.
— what do you mean, sort out?

10:00.684 --> 10:02.937
What do you mean?
I'm not supposed to be here!

10:03.020 --> 10:05.981
I'm not supposed to be here!
Open this door!

10:06.065 --> 10:08.567
Open this door! — [man] Hey!

10:11.487 --> 10:13.489
Hey, hey.

10:17.743 --> 10:21.789
It's happening to you too, isn't it?

10:41.267 --> 10:44.061
[Shouting]

10:57.700 --> 11:00.953
What's happening to Desmond?
Your friends know what's wrong.

11:01.036 --> 11:04.498
If they do, they're not sharing.
— we'll share we took off at dusk

11:04.582 --> 11:06.792
and landed in the middle of the day.

11:09.461 --> 11:12.965
Listen, I don't know
what's happening to your buddy.

11:13.048 --> 11:15.551
But you gotta trust me
when I tell you this:

11:15.634 --> 11:17.845
I am trying to help you.

11:17.970 --> 11:21.223
You want to help me?
Give me your phone.

11:21.307 --> 11:23.475
Let me call my people.

11:23.642 --> 11:26.562
You give me that weapon,
and I'll give you this phone.

11:34.570 --> 11:37.823
Be quick.
Don't go trying to call Baghdad.

11:37.907 --> 11:40.034
Those phones only call each other.

11:42.244 --> 11:45.289
[Phone ringing]

11:46.457 --> 11:48.083
[Phone beeps]

11:48.167 --> 11:50.920
Hello? — Jack, it's Sayid.

11:51.003 --> 11:52.796
I'm on the freighter.

11:52.880 --> 11:54.882
Are you ok? Where have you been?

11:54.965 --> 11:57.426
Something happened during the flight...

11:57.509 --> 11:59.803
And now Desmond's in their sick bay.

11:59.887 --> 12:02.431
Hold on, hold on, hold on, hold on.

12:02.514 --> 12:04.391
All right, you're on speaker.

12:04.516 --> 12:07.227
On the helicopter,
something happened to Desmond.

12:07.311 --> 12:10.230
He doesn't appear to recognize me
or know where he is.

12:12.191 --> 12:13.400
Side effects?

12:15.861 --> 12:17.613
Wait, your friend Desmond,

12:17.696 --> 12:21.951
has he recently been exposed
to high levels of radiation

12:22.034 --> 12:24.036
or electromagnetism?

12:27.206 --> 12:28.958
Ok, look, we don't know why,

12:29.041 --> 12:31.168
but going to and coming from the island

12:31.251 --> 12:34.964
some people can get a little confused.

12:35.047 --> 12:38.258
So, what, is this amnesia?

12:41.929 --> 12:43.847
No. This is not amnesia.

12:46.058 --> 12:48.268
Hey. Hey.

12:48.394 --> 12:51.021
Hey! Can you hear me?

12:52.189 --> 12:53.440
Are you all right?

12:58.862 --> 13:01.240
I was just on a Ferris wheel.

13:05.369 --> 13:10.582
See, ray? I'm not crazy.
It's happening to him too, ray.

13:11.750 --> 13:13.293
It's gonna happen to you.

13:13.377 --> 13:15.254
It's gonna happen to all of us.

13:15.337 --> 13:18.382
Everyone. Once we start heading
to that island again.

13:18.465 --> 13:20.551
Would you please step aside?

13:21.176 --> 13:23.679
No, no... ray, no.

13:23.762 --> 13:25.681
I need you to relax for a minute.

13:25.764 --> 13:29.143
No! No, it's not gonna stop it, ray.
Nothing can stop it, ray!

13:29.226 --> 13:31.145
Nothing can stop this...!

13:36.692 --> 13:39.778
And how are you feeling?
— what the bloody hell is going on?!

13:39.862 --> 13:43.365
I understand you're disoriented...
— you won't stick me with that!

13:43.449 --> 13:45.659
I don't want to stick you with anything.

13:45.743 --> 13:48.370
If it's ok, I just want
to check your eyes.

13:50.622 --> 13:53.834
Why? — so I can help you.

14:04.511 --> 14:05.846
What's your name?

14:08.515 --> 14:09.892
Desmond.

14:11.977 --> 14:13.145
Desmond.

14:15.814 --> 14:18.014
Why don't you tell me about
the last thing you remember?

14:40.589 --> 14:43.175
[Dial tones]

14:45.427 --> 14:48.013
[Ringing]

14:51.100 --> 14:52.559
[Woman] Hello?

14:54.436 --> 14:56.021
Penny?

14:58.315 --> 14:59.983
What do you want, Desmond?

15:01.318 --> 15:02.903
Penny, listen, I'm...

15:03.695 --> 15:05.781
I'm in trouble.

15:05.864 --> 15:08.784
I think...
I think something's happened to me.

15:09.618 --> 15:13.455
I'm confused and...
I need to see you.

15:15.874 --> 15:18.627
You broke off with me
and then you joined the army,

15:18.710 --> 15:22.798
and now you call with some expectation
I still care about you?

15:22.881 --> 15:25.467
Yeah, I'd say you are confused,
Desmond.

15:25.551 --> 15:27.719
No, I'm not. It's...

15:27.803 --> 15:30.764
Look, I've got two days leave
starting tonight.

15:32.015 --> 15:34.351
Can I... can I come and see you?
— no.

15:34.434 --> 15:37.938
No. And don't bother showing up
at the flat either. I've moved.

15:39.398 --> 15:41.275
It doesn't matter.

15:41.358 --> 15:44.778
Look, Desmond, I'm going to go.

15:44.862 --> 15:47.781
Please don't call me again.
— no, listen, penny, I...

15:47.865 --> 15:48.866
Need you.

15:53.245 --> 15:56.165
Did you just experience something,
Desmond?

15:59.084 --> 16:02.546
Frank, you're not supposed
to be here, definitely not with him.

16:02.629 --> 16:06.008
Sorry, but I got Faraday calling.
He needs to talk to this guy...

16:06.091 --> 16:10.179
Faraday's not talking to my patient.
— he's not your patient!

16:10.262 --> 16:11.847
Give Desmond the phone.

16:11.930 --> 16:14.766
[Alarm blares]
— give him the phone now!

16:16.810 --> 16:17.853
[Phone beeps]

16:19.855 --> 16:21.732
Hello? — Desmond.

16:21.815 --> 16:25.986
Desmond, my name is Daniel Faraday.
We met yesterday before you took off,

16:26.069 --> 16:28.405
but I'm guessing
you don't remember that.

16:28.488 --> 16:30.908
Took off... what?
— we don't have long to talk,

16:30.991 --> 16:34.494
so I need you to tell me
what year you think it is.

16:34.578 --> 16:37.456
What do you mean what year
do I think...? It's 1996.

16:37.539 --> 16:38.624
[Alarm continues]

16:42.085 --> 16:46.340
All right. Desmond, look,
you gotta tell me, where are you?

16:46.423 --> 16:49.343
I'm... I'm in some kind of sick bay.
— [alarm continues]

16:49.426 --> 16:52.554
No, not right now, Desmond.
Where are you supposed to be?

16:52.638 --> 16:54.681
Where are you in 1996?

16:54.765 --> 16:57.809
I'm at camp millar.
It's a royal Scots regiment.

16:57.893 --> 16:59.686
It's just north of Glasgow.

16:59.770 --> 17:02.898
Dan, you might...
— no, no, I'm thinking, I'm thinking.

17:04.149 --> 17:07.152
Desmond, listen,
when it happens again,

17:07.236 --> 17:08.820
I need you to get on a train.

17:09.571 --> 17:11.240
Get on a train and go to Oxford,

17:11.323 --> 17:15.035
Oxford university, queen's college
physics department.

17:15.118 --> 17:17.079
What? Why?

17:18.413 --> 17:21.708
Because I need you to find me.

17:28.298 --> 17:30.342
Where is it? Where is it?
— what?

17:30.425 --> 17:31.927
My journal, my journal.

17:32.010 --> 17:34.221
I need my journal,
or I won't believe him.

17:34.346 --> 17:37.557
Why does he think he's in 1996?
— I don't know.

17:37.641 --> 17:39.643
It's unpredictable.
It's a random effect.

17:39.726 --> 17:42.771
Sometimes the displacement's
a couple hours, sometimes years.

17:42.854 --> 17:44.898
Wait, this has happened before?

17:45.023 --> 17:47.859
The phone, now, please. Thank you.

17:47.943 --> 17:50.570
Desmond, are you still there?
— [man] Hey, doc!

17:50.696 --> 17:52.656
Talk to him! I can't hold them for long.

17:52.739 --> 17:55.200
[Pounding] — yes! Yes, I'm here.

17:55.284 --> 17:58.078
Ok, listen, when you find me
at queen's college,

17:58.161 --> 18:02.124
I need you to tell me
to set the device to 2.342.

18:02.207 --> 18:05.043
- What?
- [Daniel] You got it? 2.342.

18:05.127 --> 18:07.587
It must be oscillating at 11 hertz.

18:07.671 --> 18:12.926
You got it, Desmond?
— 2.342. Oscillate...

18:13.010 --> 18:16.680
[Daniel] Just remember that.
2.342 at 11 hertz, all right?

18:16.763 --> 18:20.684
One more thing, Desmond.
If the numbers don't convince me

18:20.767 --> 18:24.730
I need you to tell me
that you know about Eloise.

18:26.732 --> 18:28.066
Hey! Hey! Hey!

18:28.150 --> 18:29.693
Easy, easy!

18:29.776 --> 18:32.446
[Daniel] Desmond? Tell me
that you know about Eloise...

18:48.670 --> 18:50.672
[Church bells ringing]

18:59.473 --> 19:01.600
[Man talking]

19:03.477 --> 19:07.522
Original, the opposite of derivative.

19:07.606 --> 19:10.776
I am the one for you to impress,
Mr. Hollister.

19:10.859 --> 19:14.404
I'm not impressed.
So go, go try again.

19:16.782 --> 19:19.326
Sorry. Are you Daniel Faraday?

19:20.744 --> 19:24.539
You are?
— uh... sorry. I'm Desmond hume,

19:24.664 --> 19:27.125
and I was told I could find you here.

19:27.876 --> 19:31.671
I think I've... just been to the future.

19:35.008 --> 19:36.218
The future? — yes.

19:36.301 --> 19:41.640
I spoke to you there. You told me
to come here to Oxford to find you.

19:42.641 --> 19:44.309
You said you'd help me.

19:44.393 --> 19:47.354
Why didn't I just help you there,
in the future?

19:47.437 --> 19:48.855
Sorry?

19:48.980 --> 19:52.192
Why would I put you through
the headache of time travel.

19:52.275 --> 19:55.737
You know what I mean?
It just seems a little unnecessary.

19:57.155 --> 20:00.909
Don't you think my esteemed colleagues
could have come up with something

20:00.992 --> 20:02.661
just a little more believable?

20:02.744 --> 20:07.499
What kind of a prank is that?
Time paradox. So uninspired.

20:09.960 --> 20:12.421
Set your device to...

20:12.504 --> 20:16.091
2.342 and make sure
it oscillates at 11.

20:23.682 --> 20:29.396
Ok, now, you... you're gonna tell me
who told you those numbers.

20:31.565 --> 20:34.109
Wait a second. This is ridiculous.

20:34.192 --> 20:36.528
I know about Eloise.

20:50.041 --> 20:53.962
This is where I do the things
Oxford frowns upon.

20:54.963 --> 20:58.175
All right, this future version of me,

20:58.258 --> 21:00.760
he referenced this meeting, right?

21:00.844 --> 21:05.307
Obviously. So I would remember
you coming to Oxford, right?

21:05.390 --> 21:07.476
I would remember this here right now.

21:07.559 --> 21:09.561
Actually... no.

21:09.644 --> 21:12.564
No. — maybe you just forgot.

21:13.565 --> 21:15.650
Yeah, right. How would that happen?

21:17.027 --> 21:19.362
So this is changing the future?

21:19.446 --> 21:21.323
You can't change the future.

21:21.406 --> 21:23.742
What's that for? — radiation.

21:24.784 --> 21:26.453
[Electronic squeaking]

21:26.536 --> 21:28.330
Do I get one?
— you don't need one.

21:28.413 --> 21:31.374
It's for prolonged exposure.
I do this 20 times a day.

21:32.209 --> 21:33.919
So, what do you put on your head?

21:34.794 --> 21:36.296
[Laughs]

21:41.259 --> 21:43.303
[Beeping]

21:47.265 --> 21:49.893
This is Eloise.

21:58.360 --> 22:00.862
What does this do? — this,

22:00.946 --> 22:03.323
if the numbers you gave me are correct,

22:03.406 --> 22:05.200
what this will do...

22:05.283 --> 22:09.788
Is unstick Eloise in time,
just like you.

22:26.972 --> 22:29.558
What happened?
— wait. She's not back yet.

22:33.645 --> 22:36.606
There she is. Ok.

22:36.690 --> 22:39.317
Here goes everything.

22:41.194 --> 22:43.405
Come on, come on. Come on.

22:45.323 --> 22:48.952
That's it. Come on. That's it.

22:50.954 --> 22:52.414
Yes, yes.

22:55.333 --> 22:56.751
[Laughs]

23:03.258 --> 23:06.886
It worked! This is incredible.

23:06.970 --> 23:09.848
How is a rat running through a maze
so incredible?

23:11.641 --> 23:14.894
Is I just finished the maze
this morning.

23:14.978 --> 23:19.858
I'm not gonna teach her how to run it
until an hour from now.

23:26.990 --> 23:32.037
So you sent her to the future?
— no, her consciousness. Her mind.

23:34.706 --> 23:36.625
So how does that help me?

23:36.708 --> 23:38.960
You? Help you?

23:39.044 --> 23:41.963
I don't understand. Didn't I send you
back here to help me?

23:42.047 --> 23:43.965
I don't know why you sent me here.

23:44.049 --> 23:47.218
All I know about you is you end up
on some bloody island.

23:50.889 --> 23:52.807
What island? Why would I go to an...?

23:52.891 --> 23:54.434
Desmond, give me the phone.

23:54.517 --> 23:55.894
[Alarm blaring]

23:55.977 --> 23:57.812
Come on, everybody relax! Listen!

23:57.896 --> 24:01.691
Daniel wanted to talk to the guy,
so we brought him the phone, that's all.

24:01.775 --> 24:04.819
You let Faraday talk to him?
— he said he could help.

24:04.903 --> 24:07.781
Faraday can't even help himself!
— outside now.

24:07.906 --> 24:11.368
The captain wants to talk to you.
— I want to talk to your captain.

24:11.451 --> 24:12.994
I'll be sure to let him know.

24:13.078 --> 24:14.788
In the meantime have a seat.

24:21.461 --> 24:23.922
I need to get back.
— back where? The island?

24:24.047 --> 24:27.008
He said he could help me,
tell me what I needed to do.

24:27.092 --> 24:29.678
Desmond, can you please
explain to me...?

24:29.761 --> 24:30.929
[Man] Desmond?

24:31.012 --> 24:33.306
You're Desmond?

24:34.724 --> 24:35.892
Do I know you?

24:37.143 --> 24:38.937
I'm George minkowski.

24:39.020 --> 24:41.856
I'm the communications officer.

24:41.940 --> 24:44.109
Before they strapped me down here,

24:44.192 --> 24:48.238
all the calls to and from this boat
came through me in the radio room.

24:49.114 --> 24:51.116
And every so often...

24:51.199 --> 24:55.912
I get this flashing light
on my console.

24:55.995 --> 25:01.042
An incoming call. We were under
strict orders never to answer it.

25:03.044 --> 25:05.004
So? What's that got to do with me?

25:05.088 --> 25:07.382
Those calls came from your girlfriend.

25:09.300 --> 25:11.136
Penelope Widmore.

25:23.773 --> 25:26.359
What happened?
— ooo! You're back.

25:26.443 --> 25:29.988
And you were out almost 75 minutes.

25:30.739 --> 25:32.031
- Out? — oh, yeah.

25:32.115 --> 25:35.368
You just went catatonic
right in the middle of a sentence.

25:35.452 --> 25:39.831
I carried you to the chair. I take it
you were in the future again?

25:41.124 --> 25:44.043
For how long?
— I don't know. Five minutes.

25:47.672 --> 25:49.591
Why does this keep happening?

25:49.674 --> 25:53.344
In your case, I'm guessing
the progression is exponential.

25:54.846 --> 25:58.600
Each time your consciousness jumps
it's harder to jump back.

25:58.683 --> 26:01.895
I would be careful crossing the street
if I were you.

26:08.359 --> 26:09.611
What happened to her?

26:09.694 --> 26:12.280
She died. — I can see that. How?

26:12.363 --> 26:14.199
Brain aneurysm, probably.

26:14.282 --> 26:16.284
I'm gonna do an autopsy later.

26:17.368 --> 26:21.498
Is that gonna happen to me?
— the effects vary from case to case.

26:22.165 --> 26:26.503
Answer me! If this keeps happening,
am I gonna die?

26:28.379 --> 26:29.631
I don't know.

26:35.512 --> 26:39.265
I think Eloise's brain short—circuited.

26:40.183 --> 26:42.685
The jumps between the present
and the future,

26:42.769 --> 26:46.397
she eventually... couldn't tell
which was which. She had no anchor.

26:46.523 --> 26:50.527
What do you mean "anchor?"
— something familiar in both times.

26:50.610 --> 26:52.487
See this? This is all variables.

26:52.570 --> 26:56.324
It's random, it's chaotic.
Every equation needs stability,

26:56.407 --> 27:00.870
something known. It's called a constant.
Desmond, you have no constant.

27:02.539 --> 27:05.291
You go to the future
nothing there is familiar.

27:05.416 --> 27:07.710
So if you want to stop this...

27:08.419 --> 27:11.339
Then you need to find
something there,

27:11.422 --> 27:15.093
something that you really,
really care about...

27:16.553 --> 27:19.973
That also exists back here in 1996.

27:24.352 --> 27:25.353
This constant...

27:27.313 --> 27:29.357
Can it be a person?

27:30.149 --> 27:31.693
Yeah, maybe.

27:31.776 --> 27:34.237
But you have to make
some kind of contact.

27:35.572 --> 27:39.033
I thought you said you were off
on a boat, middle of nowhere?

27:43.580 --> 27:46.624
Who are you calling?
— I'm calling my bloody constant.

27:46.708 --> 27:47.834
[Beeping over phone]

27:47.917 --> 27:50.628
[Woman] The number you have dialed
has been disconnected.

27:56.467 --> 27:58.469
Hey, hey, are you ok?

28:04.642 --> 28:07.353
You look a lot older now, huh?

28:08.730 --> 28:11.190
Welcome back, Desmond.

28:11.274 --> 28:12.483
I need to call penny.

28:12.567 --> 28:15.153
Calling your girlfriend
is not our priority.

28:15.236 --> 28:18.406
Listen, brother, I don't know you
but you seem to know me,

28:18.489 --> 28:21.659
so if you and me are friends...

28:21.784 --> 28:23.453
Then I need your help.

28:23.536 --> 28:25.413
I need to call penny now.

28:25.496 --> 28:27.999
Whoa, you boys are getting
way ahead of yourselves.

28:28.082 --> 28:30.752
Two days ago someone
sabotaged all the equipment.

28:30.835 --> 28:34.255
We lost all communication
with the mainland.

28:34.380 --> 28:37.091
I probably could've fixed it,
but then...

28:37.175 --> 28:39.802
Then I went nuts.
— where's the radio room?

28:39.886 --> 28:43.222
It's one deck up. I'll take you there.

28:43.306 --> 28:44.682
Come on.

28:46.643 --> 28:48.436
How do we get out of here?

28:49.270 --> 28:50.980
Through the door.

28:54.525 --> 28:57.654
Looks like you guys
have a friend on this boat.

29:05.286 --> 29:06.454
Hey, your...

29:08.873 --> 29:09.999
Your nose, brother.

29:15.922 --> 29:17.840
It's clear.

29:18.174 --> 29:19.175
Let's...

29:35.233 --> 29:38.236
[Man] The black rock set sail
from Portsmouth, england

29:38.361 --> 29:43.241
march 22, 1845 on a trading mission
to the kingdom of siam

29:43.366 --> 29:45.827
when she was tragically lost at sea.

29:45.910 --> 29:48.496
The only known artifact of this journey

29:48.579 --> 29:50.999
is the journal of the ship's first mate,

29:51.082 --> 29:55.044
which was discovered among the artifacts
of pirates on I'ile sainte Marie

29:55.128 --> 29:56.170
seven years later.

29:57.296 --> 30:00.675
The contents of this journal
have never been made public

30:00.758 --> 30:04.137
to anyone outside the family
of the seller, tovard Hanso.

30:04.220 --> 30:06.889
We open the bidding on lot 2342

30:06.973 --> 30:09.517
at £150,000.

30:10.268 --> 30:12.270
One—hundred—fifty thousand, sir.

30:12.353 --> 30:16.524
To 160? Do I hear...?
One—sixty, sir. One—seventy, sir.

30:16.607 --> 30:19.527
One—eighty on the phone.
Two hundred thousand pounds.

30:19.610 --> 30:22.405
Two—hundred—twenty thousand
pounds. Two—forty?

30:22.488 --> 30:26.284
Two—hundred—sixty thousand
pounds, sir. Two—eighty?

30:26.409 --> 30:29.120
On the phone I have 300,000...
Three—twenty.

30:29.245 --> 30:32.248
Three—hundred—forty thousand pounds.
Three—sixty?

30:32.331 --> 30:36.335
Three—eighty.
— this auction's by appointment only.

30:36.419 --> 30:37.879
Do I hear £400,000?

30:37.962 --> 30:40.840
Listen, I just need to speak to...
— I'm sorry, sir.

30:41.883 --> 30:46.429
Sold, for £380,000 to bidder 755.

30:46.512 --> 30:49.348
Thank you, sir.
— just for a minute, all right?

30:49.474 --> 30:52.351
Look... Mr. Widmore. — Desmond.

30:52.435 --> 30:53.895
Can I have a word, sir?

30:53.978 --> 30:56.481
[Man] I'm sorry, Mr. Widmore...
— that's fine.

31:07.825 --> 31:10.078
Your word. Let's have it.

31:13.581 --> 31:15.583
I need to get in touch with penny.

31:16.626 --> 31:20.713
I don't know how to reach her,
and her number's been disconnected.

31:22.507 --> 31:26.886
There was a time when, if you'd asked
her to marry you, she'd have said yes.

31:27.011 --> 31:28.930
But fortunately...

31:29.013 --> 31:31.432
Your cowardice won out instead.

31:37.772 --> 31:40.483
I take it you've had second thoughts.

31:43.444 --> 31:45.988
And you'd like her to give you
another chance.

31:47.031 --> 31:48.366
Why do you hate me so much?

31:48.449 --> 31:51.828
[Chuckles] It's not me who hates you.

31:54.205 --> 31:56.457
Here's her address.

31:57.959 --> 32:00.378
I'll let her tell you herself.

32:06.175 --> 32:08.219
[Water running]

32:18.604 --> 32:20.148
Desmond.

32:22.817 --> 32:24.652
I know. It's getting harder.

32:24.735 --> 32:27.864
It starts happening faster too.

32:29.157 --> 32:30.658
Come on, let's move.

32:33.828 --> 32:36.122
Hey, how did this happen to you?

32:37.165 --> 32:38.875
We were anchored here,

32:38.958 --> 32:42.920
waiting for our orders,
bored out of our minds.

32:44.088 --> 32:46.591
Me and Brandon,
he's one of the crew members,

32:46.716 --> 32:48.968
we took out the ship's tender.

32:50.386 --> 32:52.555
We just wanted to see the island.

32:52.638 --> 32:55.349
But Brandon started acting crazy.

32:56.601 --> 32:58.186
So we had to turn around.

32:58.269 --> 33:01.439
Where is he? — in a body bag.

33:10.781 --> 33:13.993
Who did this? — you got me.

33:14.076 --> 33:16.621
But when the captain finds out,
I feel sorry...

33:21.125 --> 33:24.921
After your call, someone has to tell me
precisely what is going on.

33:27.757 --> 33:30.801
Can you fix it, brother?
— I need a minute.

33:33.137 --> 33:35.264
Do you have the number
to make the call?

33:36.641 --> 33:40.228
George, wake up, wake up.
You're going to come back.

33:40.311 --> 33:42.647
Desmond, do you know the number?

33:45.942 --> 33:48.152
No.
— well, you better remember it.

33:58.913 --> 34:01.332
I didn't realize
it was almost Christmas.

34:01.415 --> 34:03.125
It's been...

34:03.751 --> 34:05.253
Desmond.

34:14.178 --> 34:16.222
I... can't...

34:16.305 --> 34:18.849
Get... back.

34:30.820 --> 34:32.488
What happened to him?

34:35.616 --> 34:38.744
The same thing
that's gonna happen to me.

35:36.135 --> 35:37.178
Desmond?

35:39.013 --> 35:41.307
What are you doing here?
— I had to.

35:41.390 --> 35:44.477
I tried to call you,
but you disconnected your phone.

35:44.560 --> 35:46.228
Yeah, because I moved.

35:47.396 --> 35:49.482
I don't know if you're
getting the signals,

35:49.565 --> 35:52.360
but I'm trying to make a clean break.
So if you don't mind...

35:52.443 --> 35:55.488
Wait, wait, wait. Please, I just need
to get your new phone number.

35:55.571 --> 35:58.574
Why would I give you that?
— I made a huge mistake.

35:58.657 --> 36:02.203
I should never have broken up with you.
I know that now, I'm sorry.

36:02.286 --> 36:04.705
Don't. Just don't do this.
— I understand.

36:04.789 --> 36:07.708
I know it's too late to change things,

36:07.792 --> 36:10.419
but I need to tell you something.

36:10.503 --> 36:14.048
I need you to listen to me.
I know it's gonna sound ridiculous,

36:14.131 --> 36:16.717
but... please, pen.

36:18.302 --> 36:20.137
I need you to listen to me.

36:29.313 --> 36:31.482
Just say what you need
to say and then go.

36:33.651 --> 36:37.321
I know this doesn't make sense
because it doesn't make sense to me.

36:37.405 --> 36:39.657
But eight years from now...

36:41.492 --> 36:42.701
I need to call you.

36:42.785 --> 36:46.205
And I can't call you
if I don't have your number.

36:47.456 --> 36:50.167
What?
— penny, just give me your number.

36:50.334 --> 36:53.421
I know I've ruined things. I know
you think things are over,

36:53.504 --> 36:57.550
but they're not. If there's any part of
you that still believes in us, just...

36:57.675 --> 37:01.011
Give me your number.
— what's to say you won't call tonight?

37:01.095 --> 37:05.516
I won't call... for eight years.

37:07.852 --> 37:10.354
December 24, 2004.

37:11.522 --> 37:12.690
Christmas Eve.

37:15.067 --> 37:16.527
I promise.

37:19.530 --> 37:21.157
Please, pen.

37:24.368 --> 37:26.829
If I give you the number,
will you leave?

37:43.179 --> 37:45.723
All that, and you're not gonna
write it down?

37:48.684 --> 37:50.436
It wouldn't do any good.

37:52.062 --> 37:54.231
You have to keep that number.

37:54.315 --> 37:58.110
Get out! Get out!
— just remember, December 24, 2004.

37:58.194 --> 38:00.905
If you still care about me,
you have to answer.

38:00.988 --> 38:03.741
I'm not crazy, penny!
You have to believe me! You have to...

38:03.824 --> 38:05.743
Trust me.

38:05.868 --> 38:07.828
I do trust you.

38:07.912 --> 38:10.456
But you still have to remember
that number.

38:16.837 --> 38:19.298
7946—0893. It's a London number.

38:19.381 --> 38:20.674
Excellent timing.

38:22.092 --> 38:24.053
The patch is done,

38:24.136 --> 38:26.722
but I don't know how long
the battery will last.

38:29.975 --> 38:31.268
I hope she's there.

38:32.061 --> 38:33.562
I hope so too.

39:10.474 --> 39:12.476
[Penny over phone] Hello?

39:14.436 --> 39:16.772
Penny?

39:16.855 --> 39:18.524
[Penny] Desmond?

39:30.035 --> 39:32.037
Penny. Penny, you answered.

39:33.706 --> 39:35.124
You answered, penny.

39:38.586 --> 39:39.878
Des, where are you?

39:44.675 --> 39:47.595
I'm... I'm on a boat...

39:49.513 --> 39:52.308
I've... I've been on an island and...

39:54.602 --> 39:57.354
Oh, my god, penny, is that really you?
— yeah.

39:58.314 --> 39:59.315
Yes, it's me.

40:02.526 --> 40:03.652
You believed me.

40:05.654 --> 40:08.365
You still care about me.

40:08.449 --> 40:11.910
Des, I've been looking for you
for the past three years.

40:11.994 --> 40:15.372
I know about the island.
I've been researching...

40:17.875 --> 40:20.461
And then when I spoke
to your friend Charlie,

40:20.544 --> 40:24.882
that's when I knew you were still alive.
That's when I knew! Wasn't crazy.

40:25.507 --> 40:27.968
[Static]

40:28.052 --> 40:30.554
Des, are you still there?
— yes, yes, I'm here.

40:30.638 --> 40:33.849
I'm still here. Can you hear me?
— yeah, that's better.

40:34.725 --> 40:36.977
I love you, penny.

40:39.647 --> 40:41.315
I've always loved you.

40:43.400 --> 40:44.610
I'm so sorry.

40:47.321 --> 40:49.406
I love you.

40:49.490 --> 40:50.532
I love you too.

40:51.367 --> 40:53.369
I don't know where I am.
— I'll find you.

40:53.452 --> 40:55.496
I promise... I'll come back.
— no matter what.

40:55.579 --> 40:57.706
I won't give up, I promise.
— I promise.

40:57.790 --> 40:59.208
I love you. — I love you.

40:59.291 --> 41:01.585
[Static]

41:10.344 --> 41:13.806
I'm sorry. The power source
went dead. That's all we had.

41:23.941 --> 41:26.235
Thank you, Sayid.

41:30.781 --> 41:32.491
It was enough.

41:35.369 --> 41:37.287
Are you all right now?

41:42.459 --> 41:44.169
I'm perfect.
